2026-09-02T08:30:00.000Z note (out-of-band: run 1 was ABORTED at the human gate, and the cause is an agent contract violation rather than an engine or flow defect. head-of-product returned verdict=ready having composed an eleven-criterion document — its `summary` in .quorum/runs/Q-0097-1/steps/003-head-of-product/output.txt describes the whole of it, including two findings of its own and a ruling on its own OQ-2 — but wrote `"document":"gate obligations only — see document body"` into the field the engine persists, against an output contract that says in as many words "Put the complete markdown document in `document`". So requirements/merged.md and requirements/run-1/merged-iter-1.md are both 44 bytes and the merged requirement does not exist. `advance` would have been the PM owner approving a document that is not there, and the gate offers no third answer: runGate honours `retry` only where `step.retryTarget` is set, which is an exhaustion gate alone, so the spike CLI itself prints "advance / abort". $7.587 billed to claude across two steps plus 104,178 codex tokens unpriced, and nothing recoverable was lost — both candidates survive under requirements/run-1/ at 46 KB (claude) and 16 KB (codex). requirements/merged.md was removed before run 2 rather than left in place, because head-of-product reads it as an input and the placeholder carries no information; merged-iter-1.md is kept as the evidence.)
2026-09-02T08:30:30.000Z note (out-of-band: registered and NOT fixed here — nothing validates that a step's document is substantive. A step can satisfy its schema, return `ready`, write a 44-byte placeholder to every path in `output.writes`, and reach a human gate looking green; the engine writes an agent's document verbatim and asks nothing of it. That is "a check that skips its subject must not report success" (2026-08-25) arriving one layer up, on the artifact rather than on the check. Reported rather than opened as a successor, per "resolve rather than open a successor": it is not this ticket's subject, it wants its own requirement — what a minimum is, whether it is per-step or per-flow, and whether the engine or `harness lint` owns it — and Q-0097 must not acquire an engine change on the way past.)
